     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. At that level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nHere are some things you may have meant:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** at a different frequency.\n\nPlease tell me the intended dose and frequency, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate and should be entered as written. I'll enter the order as soon as I hear back."
      }
     ],
